  "methodology": "Normal-sign convention: every reported unit normal points toward INCREASING u (it is grad u / |grad u| of the reconstructed field). Signed normal speeds use this convention: positive = the front moves toward the higher-value side. Both fitted fronts move toward the lower-left (decreasing x+y): s1 ~ 0.25 (high/mid front) and s2 ~ 1.7 (mid/low front), fitted globally from each observation's actual timestamp (no time-binning bias). Reconstruction: the global two-front logistic model (16-start Levenberg-Marquardt over all 1164 observations) evaluated on the 128x128 grid at each evaluation timestamp with front width 0.08 (the data only bound the true width from above, ~0.05; the mid-level curve is insensitive to this). Curves: marching squares at the mid-levels between adjacent plateau values. Residuals in this report: |model - u_obs| for the 482 observations within 0.6 of a front at their own timestamp; pass_fraction_20pct = fraction with |resid| <= 20% of the local jump (jumps sampled consistently at p +/- 0.5*n on the reconstruction). Confidence formula: 1 - max(0, fit_rms - noise)/(0.2 * mean jump), clipped to [0.01, 0.99]."
